      "message": "Now that the script calls git_cl in-process, several pieces aren\u0027t needed anymore:\n\n1. **The retry loop in `fetch_try_results()`.** gerrit_util already retries up to 6 times with backoff (`TRY_LIMIT`), so this loop multiplies that by 3. That\u0027s part of why a 404 hangs for minutes. Please drop the loop, and the broad `except` (`TypeError`/`KeyError` there would hide bugs).\n2. **`_extract_patchset_from_tags()`.** `_fetch_tryjobs` queries a single patchset, so every build is on `resolved_ps`. Return it from `fetch_try_results()` instead of parsing tags.\n3. **`get_current_branch_cl()` running `git cl issue` and regex-parsing its output.** `git_cl.Changelist()` with no args gives `GetIssue()` and `GetCodereviewServer()` for the current branch directly.\n4. **`parse_cl_arg()` next to `_parse_cl_arg_with_project()`.** Only the tests use the 3-tuple wrapper; one function is enough.\n5. **`_normalize_gerrit_host()` runs three times** (on the whole URL, in `find_cl_builds()`, and in `fetch_try_results()`). Once, on the parsed host, is enough.\n6. **`return_none_on_error`.** It\u0027s only used by monitor.py two CLs up. Either use it in `main()` to exit non-zero (see my other comment) or add it in the CL that needs it.\n7. Smaller: the `isinstance(builds, list)` check and the `explicit_ps \u003c 1` validation (argparse\u0027s `type\u003dint` and the `\\d+` regex already cover it).",
